\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Give me the faith which can remove
\par And sink the mountain to a plain;
\par Give me the child-like  praying love,
\par Which longs to build Thy house again;
\par Thy love, let it my heart o'erpower
\par And all my simple soul devour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I would the precious time  redeem,
\par And longer live for this  alone,
\par To spend, and to be spent, for them
\par Who have not yet my saviour known;
\par Fully on these my mission prove,
\par And only breathe, to breathe Thy love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My talents , gifts, and graces, Lord,
\par Into  Thy  blessed hands receive;
\par And let me live to preach Thy word,
\par And let me to Thy glory  live;
\par My every  sacred moment spend
\par In publishing the sinners'  Friend.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Enlarge, inflame, and fill my heart
\par With boundless charity divine:
\par So shall I all my strength exert,
\par And love them with a zeal like Thine,
\par And lead them to Thy open side,
\par The sheep for whom their Shepherd died.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

